{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LxsGQzwzM9nbym242wLadp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FAQ - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X\",\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026's review process, though specific reviewer guidelines and review form details are not fully detailed in these results. Here's what I found:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 Review Process Overview\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference.\n\n## Key Reviewer Requirements and Deadlines\n\nIf you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews - by July 29.\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\n## Reviewer Responsibilities\n\nACL has adopted a policy similar to that of CVPR, requiring all authors to sign up as reviewers, with assignments made based on their qualifications. Reviewers who fail to fulfill their responsibilities may become ineligible to commit or (re-)submit papers in the following ARR cycle.\n\nFor detailed information about the specific review form and comprehensive reviewer guidelines, you may want to check the official EMNLP 2026 website (2026.emnlp.org) or the ACL Rolling Review platform (aclrollingreview.org), which would have the most up-to-date and detailed reviewer guidelines and review form templates.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c935f96-e8ee-4264-8300-457f7616e2aa","uuid":"6b464480-b3b7-491e-980e-e98af0c81582","timestamp":"2026-05-16T17:25:05.375Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_016XfPsfPc9zwNsXNn2KjPzP","content":[{"title":"FAQ - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026"},{"title":"EMNLP | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X","url":"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X","url":"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026's review process, though specific reviewer guidelines and review form details are not fully detailed in these results. Here's what I found:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 Review Process Overview\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference.\n\n## Key Reviewer Requirements and Deadlines\n\nIf you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews - by July 29.\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\n## Reviewer Responsibilities\n\nACL has adopted a policy similar to that of CVPR, requiring all authors to sign up as reviewers, with assignments made based on their qualifications. Reviewers who fail to fulfill their responsibilities may become ineligible to commit or (re-)submit papers in the following ARR cycle.\n\nFor detailed information about the specific review form and comprehensive reviewer guidelines, you may want to check the official EMNLP 2026 website (2026.emnlp.org) or the ACL Rolling Review platform (aclrollingreview.org), which would have the most up-to-date and detailed reviewer guidelines and review form templates."],"durationSeconds":4.961458069}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LqnFsqGMgN4uZGaAXPLMzi","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"Surviving ARR May Meta-Review & Deciding on EMNLP 2025: A Tactical and Honest Guide | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/113/surviving-arr-may-meta-review-deciding-on-emnlp-2025-a-tactical-and-honest-guide\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ\"},{\"title\":\"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters\"},{\"title\":\"Automatically Measuring Peer Review's Utility for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1476.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper\",\"url\":\"https://cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Policies for Review and Citation - Admin Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php/ACL_Policies_for_Review_and_Citation\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines. Here's what I found:\n\n## Review Form Structure\n\nThe review form consists of four main sections, with the first being an In-Depth Review section for overall assessment of the paper and to provide evidence supporting opinions. The core review is the most important part and should include your view of the main contributions the paper intended to make and how well it succeeds, along with significant strong and weak parts.\n\n## Scoring Rubric\n\nA 5 point scale with half point increments is used. Different from ACL 2020, a rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, though reviewers should try to take a stand by selecting 2.5 or 3.5, but should use 3 if they think the paper is borderline or cannot decide.\n\n## Reproducibility Assessment\n\nReviewers must answer: \"How do you rate the paper's reproducibility? Will members of the ACL community be able to reproduce or verify the results in this paper?\" using scores of 1-5. There is also a question about whether the authors' answers to the Reproducibility Checklist are useful, with three choices provided (very useful, somewhat useful, not useful).\n\n## Important Considerations\n\nDecisions will be made not just on scores and certainly not on average scores, but will also take into account the whole review, reviewer discussion, and Area Chair meta-reviews and recommendations.\n\nThe official instructions page can be found at https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c935f96-e8ee-4264-8300-457f7616e2aa","uuid":"08e7e30b-a91f-40e2-97cb-6fb6bb0dcaa6","timestamp":"2026-05-16T17:25:08.079Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01UkDseNTR1cwMnpH8funFi2","content":[{"title":"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025","url":"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"Surviving ARR May Meta-Review & Deciding on EMNLP 2025: A Tactical and Honest Guide | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/113/surviving-arr-may-meta-review-deciding-on-emnlp-2025-a-tactical-and-honest-guide"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ"},{"title":"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters"},{"title":"Automatically Measuring Peer Review's Utility for Authors","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1476.pdf"},{"title":"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper","url":"https://cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters"},{"title":"ACL Policies for Review and Citation - Admin Wiki","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php/ACL_Policies_for_Review_and_Citation"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines. Here's what I found:\n\n## Review Form Structure\n\nThe review form consists of four main sections, with the first being an In-Depth Review section for overall assessment of the paper and to provide evidence supporting opinions. The core review is the most important part and should include your view of the main contributions the paper intended to make and how well it succeeds, along with significant strong and weak parts.\n\n## Scoring Rubric\n\nA 5 point scale with half point increments is used. Different from ACL 2020, a rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, though reviewers should try to take a stand by selecting 2.5 or 3.5, but should use 3 if they think the paper is borderline or cannot decide.\n\n## Reproducibility Assessment\n\nReviewers must answer: \"How do you rate the paper's reproducibility? Will members of the ACL community be able to reproduce or verify the results in this paper?\" using scores of 1-5. There is also a question about whether the authors' answers to the Reproducibility Checklist are useful, with three choices provided (very useful, somewhat useful, not useful).\n\n## Important Considerations\n\nDecisions will be made not just on scores and certainly not on average scores, but will also take into account the whole review, reviewer discussion, and Area Chair meta-reviews and recommendations.\n\nThe official instructions page can be found at https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/"],"durationSeconds":7.5545143029999995}}
